    "html": "<p><strong>The complaint.</strong> On September 15, 2026, Leah Goldberg, a Member Services Representative II in the Contact Center, filed a complaint about her supervisor, Marcus Doyle, Team Supervisor, Member Services. She alleged that he denied her request to avoid Friday evening shifts for Shabbat observance, did not consider a coworker's offered shift swap, and made comments suggesting disrespect for her religious practice. <button type=\"button\" class=\"source-number\" data-cite=\"synopsis\" aria-label=\"Source 1: Case synopsis, line 1\" title=\"Source 1: Case synopsis, line 1\">1</button></p>\n<p><strong>Scope.</strong> The investigation covers three allegations under two policies. Two fall under the Religious Accommodation Policy: whether Doyle responded within five business days, and whether he considered and discussed alternatives and consulted HR before denying the request. One falls under the Anti-Harassment Policy: whether Doyle made remarks about religion or Goldberg's observance.</p>\n<p><strong>Work done.</strong> Intake is complete. No interviews have taken place, and no findings have been made.</p>\n<p><strong>Status.</strong> The initial investigation plan is awaiting review. Interviews and document collection are expected to follow once the plan is approved. The next update will be provided on [date of next update].</p>",
