    "html": "<div><p>Not in the record. Kim is the only person who says he heard it himself, and he places himself about six feet from Doyle's desk after the huddle. He quotes Doyle as saying \"If everyone wanted their holy day off, nobody would work Fridays.\" <button type=\"button\" class=\"source-number\" data-cite=\"jordan\" aria-label=\"Source 1: Jordan Kim — Witness, Member Services Representative — Interview Transcript, line 55\" title=\"Source 1: Jordan Kim — Witness, Member Services Representative — Interview Transcript, line 55\">1</button></p>\n<p>Goldberg did not hear it. She says \"Not myself\" and that Kim told her afterwards. <button type=\"button\" class=\"source-number\" data-cite=\"leah\" aria-label=\"Source 2: Leah Goldberg — Complainant, Member Services Representative II — Interview Transcript, line 79\" title=\"Source 2: Leah Goldberg — Complainant, Member Services Representative II — Interview Transcript, line 79\">2</button> Rivera's notes say she did not hear Doyle say anything about Goldberg's religion. <button type=\"button\" class=\"source-number\" data-cite=\"carla\" aria-label=\"Source 3: Carla Rivera — Witness — Interview Transcript, line 15\" title=\"Source 3: Carla Rivera — Witness — Interview Transcript, line 15\">3</button></p>\n<p>Doyle is not a second hearer, but he partly confirms the remark. He says he \"might have said something like that\" and that it was about staffing in general. <button type=\"button\" class=\"source-number\" data-cite=\"marcus\" aria-label=\"Source 4: Marcus Doyle — Subject, Team Supervisor, Member Services — Interview Transcript, line 63\" title=\"Source 4: Marcus Doyle — Subject, Team Supervisor, Member Services — Interview Transcript, line 63\">4</button> So the words are largely undisputed, and the dispute is over what he meant.</p>\n<p>Kim describes Doyle as \"talking to himself, kind of loud,\" which suggests others nearby may have heard. <button type=\"button\" class=\"source-number\" data-cite=\"jordan\" aria-label=\"Source 1: Jordan Kim — Witness, Member Services Representative — Interview Transcript, line 55\" title=\"Source 1: Jordan Kim — Witness, Member Services Representative — Interview Transcript, line 55\">1</button> The record doesn't say who else was in earshot. Asking Kim who else was nearby, and checking whether any other team members were at their desks, would be the way to find out.</p></div>",
    "text": "Not in the record. Kim is the only person who says he heard it himself, and he places himself about six feet from Doyle's desk after the huddle. He quotes Doyle as saying \"If everyone wanted their holy day off, nobody would work Fridays.\" 1 Goldberg did not hear it. She says \"Not myself\" and that Kim told her afterwards. 2 Rivera's notes say she did not hear Doyle say anything about Goldberg's religion. 3 Doyle is not a second hearer, but he partly confirms the remark. He says he \"might have said something like that\" and that it was about staffing in general. 4 So the words are largely undisputed, and the dispute is over what he meant. Kim describes Doyle as \"talking to himself, kind of loud,\" which suggests others nearby may have heard. 1 The record doesn't say who else was in earshot. Asking Kim who else was nearby, and checking whether any other team members were at their desks, would be the way to find out.",
