    "html": "<div><p>The plan has only four allegations, so there is no allegation 5 to reword. I assume you mean allegation 4, which currently asks whether Doyle removed Goldberg from the escalations queue \"because she requested a religious accommodation or because she complained to HR\". If you want a new fifth allegation instead, tell me and I'll draft it that way.</p>\n<p>Here is a reworded version tied only to the September 15 complaint: <span role=\"img\" title=\"no source cited. This sentence states a fact but cites no source. Check it before relying on it.\" aria-label=\"no source cited. This sentence states a fact but cites no source. Check it before relying on it.\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg></span></p>\n<p><em>Did Marcus Doyle remove Goldberg from the escalations queue on September 16, 2026, because she filed her complaint with HR on September 15, 2026?</em></p>\n<p>This narrows the question. The accommodation-request theory drops out, though her September 4 request is protected activity under the Anti-Retaliation Policy. <button type=\"button\" class=\"source-number\" data-cite=\"retaliation-policy\" aria-label=\"Source 1: Policy: Anti-Retaliation Policy (full text, from the policy library), line 18\" title=\"Source 1: Policy: Anti-Retaliation Policy (full text, from the policy library), line 18\">1</button> The reworded allegation also turns on what Doyle knew. He says he first learned of the complaint on September 17, <button type=\"button\" class=\"source-number\" data-cite=\"marcus\" aria-label=\"Source 2: Marcus Doyle — Subject, Team Supervisor, Member Services — Interview Transcript, line 87\" title=\"Source 2: Marcus Doyle — Subject, Team Supervisor, Member Services — Interview Transcript, line 87\">2</button> and the complaint email is dated September 15 at 8:12 AM. <button type=\"button\" class=\"source-number\" data-cite=\"complaint\" aria-label=\"Source 3: 01_Complaint_Email_Goldberg.docx, line 7\" title=\"Source 3: 01_Complaint_Email_Goldberg.docx, line 7\">3</button> If you keep the request theory out, the record should say why.</p></div><p class=\"violet-followup\">The plan has only four allegations, so I took \"allegation 5\" to mean allegation 4. The card rewords it to cover only the September 15 complaint. That drops the accommodation-request theory from the plan.</p>",
